  "findings": {
    "front": "Smooth preparation, cross-foot work and return. Holding arm remains visible throughout the inward reach; head turns gradually without the earlier intermediate overturn. Both feet stay fixed and the lower silhouette is continuous.",
    "oblique": "Forward common-body reach is visible and lowers the held tool. The arm retains clearance, with no round02 distal disappearance or disconnected neck. Body returns without a second bounce.",
    "side": "The low grip and forward posture remain consistent through approach, work and recovery. Continuous lower transition and fixed sole; no abrupt local side fold observed.",
    "top": "Continuous common turn, rigid original head and tail transport. Head naturally occludes much of body/arms, so this view alone cannot certify attachment.",
    "restAndEnd": "Initial hold and final settled poses match; no visible loop seam.",
    "sourceResiduals": "Head-orientation cue and broom/mid-belly errors improve; head-envelope translation becomes smaller than the source and lowest belly edge remains under-responsive. No retiming or source-shape manipulation."
